From: rockbandPi
Subject: [PATCH] Low quality renderer without an extra copy

The Low quality URP renderer forces an intermediate texture (Always), so
every camera renders into one and then copies it to its target. Use Auto:
URP then renders straight to the target when nothing needs an intermediate.
On tile-based GPUs every full-screen copy costs real time; on the Raspberry
Pi 5 this took a song from 40 to 47 FPS.

The venue's post-processing pass reads the camera's color texture, so it
now asks URP for an intermediate texture itself (requiresIntermediateTexture).
Without that the venue fails to render ("The passed in texture handle does
not have a valid descriptor").
---
diff --git a/Assets/Script/Gameplay/VenueCameraRenderer.cs b/Assets/Script/Gameplay/VenueCameraRenderer.cs
--- a/Assets/Script/Gameplay/VenueCameraRenderer.cs
+++ b/Assets/Script/Gameplay/VenueCameraRenderer.cs
@@ -404,6 +404,9 @@
             public VenuePostPostProcessingPass(VenueCameraRenderer vcr)
             {
                 renderPassEvent = RenderPassEvent.AfterRenderingPostProcessing;
+                // Reads the camera's color texture, which needs an intermediate
+                // texture when the renderer's mode is Auto (Low quality)
+                requiresIntermediateTexture = true;
                 _alphaFixMaterial = vcr._alphaFixMaterial;
             }
 
diff --git a/Assets/Settings/Low_Renderer.asset b/Assets/Settings/Low_Renderer.asset
--- a/Assets/Settings/Low_Renderer.asset
+++ b/Assets/Settings/Low_Renderer.asset
@@ -67,4 +67,4 @@
   m_DepthAttachmentFormat: 0
   m_DepthTextureFormat: 0
   m_AccurateGbufferNormals: 0
-  m_IntermediateTextureMode: 1
+  m_IntermediateTextureMode: 0
